WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Reminders. Get a bell notification and an email before a timed task is due.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.500
Use it for: meetings; bills.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:15.000
Set a due time → Choose a lead time → Bell and email when it's due

4
00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.920
(Note: The reminder sweep was run through the scheduler route instead of waiting for the clock.) Reminders need a due time.

5
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.600
Add one…

6
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.680
…then choose when to be reminded.

7
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:29.400
When it's due, the reminder lands in the bell (and by email).

8
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:35.400
“Add a due time to set a reminder.”: Set a time under Due time (optional) first. No email arrived: The server needs SMTP for emails; the bell notification still appears.

9
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.900
Bell and email
